INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_entry` (`ID`, `Kind`, `Zone`, `SortOrder`, `Faction`, `RequiredState`, `Title`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(13000, 0, 130, 0, 0, 0, 'Silverpine Forest', 'Silverpine Forest runs along the rugged western coast of Lordaeron, a country of tall silver-barked pines between Tirisfal Glades to the north and the Greymane Wall to the south, with Lordamere Lake along its eastern edge. Its southern reaches once belonged to Gilneas, until King Genn Greymane sealed his kingdom behind the wall and left them outside. Then came the Scourge, and with it Arugal, the archmage who summoned the worgen to fight the undead. The beasts turned on the living as well, and from Shadowfang Keep above Pyrewood Village the mad wizard now calls them his children. Lady Sylvanas counts Silverpine a strategic stronghold, and from an old crypt called the Sepulcher her Forsaken struggle to hold it. Enemies press them on every side: Moonrage worgen in the woods, the rot hide gnolls and undead servants of Thule Ravenclaw on the farms and Fenris Isle, and wizards of Dalaran at work in Ambermill. Refugees still huddle at the closed gates of the wall.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Silverpine_Forest (geography, southern part originally Gilnean, Greymane Wall, Arugal and the worgen, Shadowfang above Pyrewood); quest 421 description (Varimathras, Arugal''s reckless magic, strategic stronghold); quest 1014 description; quest 1476 description (refugees refused at the Greymane Wall); quest_greeting 1952; DB spawns: Moonrage, Rot Hide, Ravenclaw, Dalaran creatures across the zone'),
(13001, 1, 130, 1, 0, 0, 'The Skittering Dark', 'Northwest of the Sepulcher lies the Skittering Dark, a gloomy corner of the forest given over to giant spiders. Moss stalkers and mist creepers spin their webs among the trees, and great grizzled bears wander the slopes around them. Even here the Forsaken see opportunity. Apothecary Renferrel of the Royal Apothecary Society has found that the blood of these spiders, mixed with a toxin drawn from the heart of a grizzled bear, yields a deadly elixir, one more ingredient in the New Plague the Dark Lady demands of his order.', 'quest 447 description (spiders in the Skittering Dark to the northwest, spider blood plus bear heart toxin); DB spawns in area 226: Moss Stalker 1780, Mist Creeper 1781, Giant Grizzled Bear 1797; quest_greeting 1937'),
(13002, 1, 130, 2, 0, 0, 'North Tide''s Run', 'North Tide''s Run is a lonely stretch of Silverpine''s sea coast, west of the Sepulcher, where the tide breaks against Lordaeron''s western shore. On it stands a shaman''s shrine whose pool has been tainted by the plague. The water spirits that once spoke there have fallen silent or been twisted into corrupt manifestations, and shamans of the Horde come to defeat the foul spirit and cleanse the pool with a ritual at the brazier beside it. Even when the corruption ebbs, they say, life in this forest goes on waning.', 'quest 63 description (shrine on the coast west of the Sepulcher, tainted by the plague); quest 100 description and reward text; quest 1103 (Tiev Mordune); DB spawns in area 305: Corrupt Water Spirit 5897, Corrupt Minor Manifestation of Water 5894, Shaman Shrine 101750, Brazier of Everfount 113791, Tiev Mordune 7007'),
(13003, 1, 130, 3, 0, 0, 'Malden''s Orchard', 'Malden''s Orchard is a farmstead in northern Silverpine, east of the Ivar Patch, and whoever once lived there is gone. Worgs now prowl its untended trees in such hungry numbers that the Deathstalker Erland, a Forsaken scout, found himself trapped in the farmhouse, eyed by the wolves every time he set foot outside the door. Among the pack roams a rarely seen worg called Gorefang. Erland''s report to his comrades was brief: masses of wolves to the east, and no trace of the people of the orchard.', 'creature_text 1978 (Erland: masses of wolves to the east, whoever lived at Malden''s Orchard is gone); quest 435 description; quest 429 description (worgs between the Ivar Patch and Malden''s Orchard to the east); DB spawns in area 238: Mottled Worg 1766, Worg 1765, Gorefang 12431 (rare), Deathstalker Erland 1978'),
(13004, 1, 130, 4, 0, 0, 'The Ivar Patch', 'The Ivar Patch is a farm in northern Silverpine, north of the Sepulcher, where shambling Ravenclaw slaves, ghouls in the service of Thule Ravenclaw, now wander the fields. Its barn is the lair of Ivar the Foul, a ghoul who fell on the Deathstalkers Rane and Quinn Yorick when they passed through on a scouting mission and mauled Quinn badly. The brother and sister now hold out in the farmhouse, Rane standing guard while Quinn recovers, and Ivar lurks in the barn waiting for her watch to slip.', 'quest 425 description (attacked by Ivar the Foul, barn yonder); quest 430 log description (Ivar Patch north of the Sepulcher); quest_greeting 1950 (holed up in this farmhouse); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Olsen''s_Farthing (Ravenclaw Slaves are ghouls under Thule); DB spawns in area 239: Ravenclaw Slave 1866 x15, Ivar the Foul 1971, Rane 1950, Quinn 1951'),
(13005, 1, 130, 5, 0, 0, 'The Dead Field', 'The Dead Field is a deserted farm in northern Silverpine whose former owners are unknown. The rot hide gnolls, servants of the Scourge, have made it a base, and every small assault the Forsaken have sent against it has been broken by the banshee Nightlash, who appears to defend the gnolls whenever they come under attack. At times an apparition of Thule Ravenclaw rises among them to stir their rage, promising that the Dark Lady''s followers will be driven from Silverpine and the war carried to their very capital.', 'quest 437 description; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/The_Dead_Field (run-down deserted farm, nothing known of its owners, Ravenclaw Apparition); creature_text 2056 (Ravenclaw Apparition); smart_scripts areatrigger 173 summons Ravenclaw Apparition 2056 at the Dead Fields; DB spawns in area 240: Rot Hide Gladerunner 1772, Rot Hide Mystic 1773, Nightlash 1983'),
(13006, 1, 130, 6, 0, 0, 'Valgan''s Field', 'Valgan''s Field is a small wheat farm on the western shore of Lordamere Lake, north of a bridge on the forest road. When the archmage Arugal first came to Silverpine he stayed here, and he left behind a stack of dusty spellbooks, among them the spell he named his Remedy. Moonrage worgen, the cursed fruit of his magic, now prowl the farm, and Vile Fin murlocs creep up from the shore. Lately the place has drawn notice from the Argent Tournament in Icecrown, where a champion called the Black Knight claims to hail from here, a story the farm itself does nothing to support.', 'quest 422 description (Arugal first stayed at the wheat farm just north of the bridge, spellbooks, Remedy of Arugal); quest 13634 description and reward text (small farm on the western shore of Lordamere Lake, Black Knight''s story a sham); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Valgan''s_Field; DB spawns in area 227: Moonrage Whitescalp, Moonrage Darkrunner, Vile Fin Shredder, Dusty Spellbooks 1571, Dusty Journal 194340'),
(13007, 1, 130, 7, 0, 0, 'The Sepulcher', 'Built into an old crypt and graveyard beside the road that crosses the forest, the Sepulcher is the Forsaken base in Silverpine and one of its few safe havens. High Executor Hadrec commands here and bats fly daily to the Undercity. Allies have come as well, an envoy of the blood elves and the tauren Mura Runetotem, who hopes to bring new life to this dying forest. In the graveyard lies the tomb of a paladin named Yuriv, its fine epitaph praising his devotion to the Light crudely scratched over with the word BETRAYER. His widow, left waiting night after night for a man who put his crusade first, wants nothing more to do with him.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/The_Sepulcher (old crypt converted into the Forsaken base, one of the few safe Horde locations, leader Hadrec); quest 6322 reward text (our bats fly there daily); quest 9189 description (Advisor Sorrelon represents the blood elves to the Forsaken); quest 3301 description (Mura Runetotem); page_text 690 (Yuriv''s Tombstone); quest 264 description and reward text; DB spawns in area 228: Hadrec 1952, Silverpine Deathguard 7489, Karos Razok 2226, Advisor Sorrelon 16288, Mura Runetotem 8385, Yuriv''s Tombstone 24776/24777'),
(13008, 1, 130, 8, 0, 0, 'Deep Elem Mine', 'Deep Elem Mine is cut into the hills southeast of the Sepulcher. Arugal let his magic spread even here, and the mine''s own former foreman, Grimson the Pale, now leads the worgen that have made its tunnels their home. Moonrage gluttons and darksouls crowd the shafts, still bound by the enchanted shackles through which Arugal strengthened his spells. The Forsaken covet the place. Dalar Dawnweaver reckons the mine would richly supply Varimathras''s advance across Silverpine, if only Grimson were dead.', 'quest 424 description and reward text (magic spread to the Deep Elem Mine in the hills to the southeast, tainted foreman Grimson the Pale); quest 423 description (shackles from Moonrage Gluttons and Darksouls); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Deep_Elem_Mine (former foreman led the worgen who made the mine their home); DB spawns in area 213: Moonrage Glutton 1779, Moonrage Darksoul 1782'),
(13009, 1, 130, 9, 0, 0, 'The Decrepit Ferry', 'On the shore of Lordamere Lake east of the Sepulcher, the Decrepit Ferry is an old landing that the Scourge have made their own. Hands of Ravenclaw and Ravenclaw champions guard it, and a boat tied up there is heaped with wrapped corpses, among them bodies stolen from the mass graves of Tirisfal. Across the water stands a matching dock on Fenris Isle, where the dead are bound. Deathstalker reports also place Fenwick Thatros, whom Varimathras believes to be a leader of the undead in Silverpine, near the old dock.', 'quest 438 description and reward text; quest 439 description and reward text (body likely from the mass graves in Tirisfal); quest 1998 description (Fenwick Thatros near the decrepit dock on Lordamere); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Fenris_Isle (Thule controls the Decrepit Ferry); DB spawns in area 237: Hand of Ravenclaw 1870, Ravenclaw Champion 1869, Corpse Laden Boat 1593; Fenwick Thatros 6570 just offshore'),
(13010, 1, 130, 10, 0, 0, 'Fenris Isle', 'Fenris Isle rises from Lordamere Lake east of the Decrepit Ferry, crowned by Fenris Keep, once a thriving military outpost of the kingdom of Lordaeron. Its people fled or died when the Scourge came. Now it is the stronghold of Thule Ravenclaw, the renegade mage who commands the rot hide gnolls, and the Forsaken name it the Scourge''s place of strength in Silverpine. Rot hide brutes, savages and plague weavers swarm its shores and halls, and in an unmarked grave by the stable lies the headless body of Thule''s own bodyguard, whose head the gnolls keep as a plaything.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Fenris_Isle (thriving military outpost of Lordaeron, abandoned when the Scourge came, Rot Hide base under Thule); quest 442 description (the Scourge''s place of strength in Silverpine); quest 443 description (Fenris Isle east of the Decrepit Ferry); quest 460 description (Alaric, grave near the stable); DB spawns in area 172: Rot Hide Brute 1939, Plague Weaver 1940, Savage 1942, Thule Ravenclaw 1947, Shallow Grave 1599'),
(13011, 1, 130, 11, 0, 0, 'The Dawning Isles', 'The Dawning Isles are a scatter of small islands out in Lordamere Lake, east of Fenris Isle. Vile Fin murlocs, tidecallers and shorecreepers among them, crowd their shores, and mossy lake creepers lumber through the shallows. The lake holds an old secret. According to the notes of Apothecary Berard, now lost to Arugal''s curse, an ancient plague once killed off all the aquatic life in Lordamere ages ago, and the moss that grows on the lake''s creatures and the rare hardened tumor of a Vile Fin murloc may yet hold the key to brewing another.', 'quest 450 description (ancient plague killed off all aquatic life in Lake Lordamere ages ago); quest 451 description (Lake Creeper and Skulker moss, Hardened Tumor from a Vile Fin, islands in Lake Lordamere); DB spawns in area 232: Vile Fin Tidecaller 1958, Vile Fin Shorecreeper 1957, Lake Creeper 1955, Elder Lake Creeper 1956'),
(13012, 1, 130, 12, 0, 0, 'Olsen''s Farthing', 'South of the Sepulcher lie the ruins of Olsen''s Farthing, once a bustling farmstead on a major trade route through the forest. A few years after the Third War it fell to the undead of Thule Ravenclaw, and it has never recovered. Skeletal Ravenclaw raiders patrol the broken fences and ghoulish Ravenclaw slaves shamble among the empty buildings, ready to fall on anyone who strays too near.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Olsen''s_Farthing (bustling farmstead on a major trade route, ruined and overrun by Thule''s undead a few years after the Third War, Raiders are skeletal warriors, Slaves are ghouls); DB spawns in area 229: Ravenclaw Raider 1865 x11, Ravenclaw Slave 1866 x10 (average position south of the Sepulcher)'),
(13013, 1, 130, 13, 0, 0, 'Pyrewood Village', 'Pyrewood Village lies in southern Silverpine beneath Shadowfang Keep, a Gilnean village of chapel, smithy and town hall left outside when the Greymane Wall went up. Arugal''s curse has given it two faces. By day its folk seem ordinary, keeping shop and standing watch; when the sun goes down they become Moonrage worgen, held by enchanted shackles. Arugal rules them through the Pyrewood Council, puppets led by Lord Mayor Morrison. Apothecary Berard kept his study at the inn before the curse took him. And when Arugal meets his end in the keep, it is here that princes of the San''layn come in the Lich King''s name to raise his shade and send it north to Solstice Village in Grizzly Hills.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Pyrewood_Village (Gilnean village, town hall, blacksmith, chapel, Lord Mayor Morrison leads the council, worgen at night); quest 99 description (human by day, Moonrage worgen at night, enchanted shackles); quest 452 description (Council as puppets); quest 450 description (Berard''s study in the Pyrewood Village Inn); creature_text 27619 (Rise, Arugal) and 27624 (sent to Solstice Village); DB spawns: Shade of Arugal 27620 and San''layn princes in area 204; Pyrewood Armorer/Tailor/Leatherworker vendors; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Archmage_Arugal (San''layn raise Arugal for the Grizzly Hills); DB spawns in area 204 (posarea): Prince Valanar 27619, Prince Atherann 27616, Shade of Arugal 27620; Keleseth 27618 and Theraldis 27624 just outside'),
(13014, 1, 130, 14, 0, 0, 'Ambermill', 'Ambermill, in southeastern Silverpine near Lordamere Lake, was a minor lumber town of mills and stables, one of the Gilnean holdings that the Greymane Wall left outside the kingdom. After the Third War wizards of the Kirin Tor occupied it, guarded by warders and protectors and supplied by crates carted up from Hillsbrad. The reason lies beneath the town. Ambermill sits on a dormant ley energy node that Dalaran once earmarked, and an archmage named Ataeric is leading the effort to wake it. To the Forsaken the town is a stubborn source of human opposition, and a vault of Dalaran''s secrets.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Ambermill (town hall, stables, mills, lumber; Kirin Tor occupied after the Third War; dormant ley node); quests 477, 482, 480 descriptions; quest 1999 description (Kirin Tor at Ambermill store documents on the state of Dalaran); DB spawns in area 233: Dalaran Warder 1913, Protector 1912, Archmage Ataeric 2120 (drops Ataeric''s Staff 3515 for quest 480); wowhead.com/classic/npc=2120 (Archmage Ataeric exists in Classic, Silverpine Forest)'),
(13015, 1, 130, 15, 0, 0, 'Beren''s Peril', 'Beren''s Peril is a cave in the hills southwest of Ambermill, not far from a pocket of Dalaran wizards. Forsaken scouts have learned that a band of undead is hiding inside: Ravenclaw guardians and drudgers in the service of Thule Ravenclaw, gathering in secret to strike at the Sepulcher. Among them lurks a rarely seen Ravenclaw Regent. Shadow Priest Allister means to turn the tables and fall on them before they are ready.', 'quest 516 description; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Beren''s_Peril (cave southwest of Ambermill, undead servants of Thule preparing an attack on the Sepulcher); DB spawns in area 231: Ravenclaw Guardian 1973, Ravenclaw Drudger 1974, Dalaran Watcher 1888; Ravenclaw Regent 2283 (rare) nearby'),
(13016, 1, 130, 16, 0, 0, 'The Greymane Wall', 'The Greymane Wall closes off the south of Silverpine, the great barrier King Genn Greymane raised to shut Gilneas away from the troubles of Lordaeron. When the Scourge massed against it, he opened the gate and sent his soldiers out, and they were slain and raised as undead. Once Arugal''s worgen turned on the Gilneans too, the gates were closed for good. Refugees from fallen Lordaeron still camp in its shadow, haggard and sickly, refused by their own kin. Dalin Forgewright tends them, the blind weaponsmith Wallace sells his blades nearby, and the murderer Valdred Moray lingers at the gate, hoping to flee into Gilneas.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Greymane_Wall (built by Genn, gate opened during the Scourging, soldiers raised, gates closed after the worgen, refugees, Dalin, Valdred, Wallace); quest 1476 description (Dalin Forgewright cares for the refugees refused by their kin); quest 530 description (Valdred at the Greymane Wall trying to flee into Gilneas); DB spawns in area 230: Haggard Refugee 2053, Sickly Refugee 2054, Dalin Forgewright 5682, Wallace the Blind 3534, Valdred Moray 2332'),
(13017, 2, 130, 1, 2, 0, 'High Executor Hadrec', 'High Executor Hadrec commands the Forsaken at the Sepulcher, and he greets every newcomer with the same blunt truth: Silverpine is saturated with enemies, and if the Forsaken are to survive they must drive them back. From his post he sends Deathstalkers to scout the northern farms, orders the assaults on the rot hide gnolls at the Dead Field, and plans the strike against their master on Fenris Isle. Even the armory has his attention, and he has the Deathguards'' lost weapons replaced from the Undercity. Hadrec admits the Scourge in Silverpine are stronger than he reckoned, and he makes sure those who help hold the line are commended.', 'quest_greeting 1952; quests 428, 437, 442 descriptions; quest 6321 description (Hadrec asked for stock of equipment); quest 449 reward text (had not accounted for the level of Scourge presence)'),
(13018, 2, 130, 2, 2, 0, 'Dalar Dawnweaver', 'Dalar Dawnweaver was an archmage of the Kirin Tor before the Scourge, and now serves the Dark Lady at the Sepulcher. He holds Arugal in open contempt: a charlatan whose spellcraft was as transparent as blown glass, who propped up weak magic with enchanted trinkets and was never fit to represent Dalaran in its darkest hour. Dalar insists he warned the Kirin Tor and was ignored. Now he studies Arugal''s spells and shackles so he can turn them against their maker and secure Silverpine for Sylvanas. He knows his old order''s secrets as well, and it was he who remembered that Ambermill sits on a dormant ley node.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dalar_Dawnweaver (former archmage of the Kirin Tor); quest_greeting 1938 (Kirin Tor did not heed my warnings); quests 422, 423 descriptions; quest 481 reward text; quest 482 description'),
(13019, 2, 130, 3, 2, 0, 'Apothecary Renferrel', 'Apothecary Renferrel of the Royal Apothecary Society keeps his station outside the Sepulcher, where he labors on the task the Dark Lady has set his order: a New Plague to bring Arthas and his army to their knees, and the human infestation with them. He brews from whatever Silverpine offers, spider blood, bear hearts, lake moss and the notes of his cursed colleague Berard, and he can spare a healing draught for a wounded Deathstalker. When the rot hide gnolls appeared, it was Renferrel who broke down their ichor and found warlock and necromantic magic within it, setting the Forsaken on the trail of Thule Ravenclaw.', 'quest_greeting 1937; quest 447 description (New Plague, Scourge Army and the Human infestation); quests 450, 451; quests 429, 430 (healing potion from worg hearts); quest 443 description (stationed outside the Sepulcher); quest 444 description'),
(13020, 2, 130, 4, 2, 0, 'Shadow Priest Allister', 'Shadow Priest Allister is the Sepulcher''s keeper of secrets. Through scouts and agents, he boasts, the Forsaken control the flow of information in Lordaeron, with every Scourge movement and holding under their watchful eyes. His chief concern is Ambermill, where the support of Dalaran''s wizards keeps human opposition alive. Allister had their supply crates searched, set agents to stripping the wizards of their pendants, and ordered the archmage overseeing the ley node slain. His scouts also uncovered Thule Ravenclaw''s undead massing at Beren''s Peril, and he sent a strike against them before they could move.', 'quest_greeting 2121; quests 477, 479, 480 descriptions and reward texts; quest 516 description and reward text'),
(13021, 2, 130, 5, 0, 0, 'Thule Ravenclaw', 'Thule Ravenclaw was a young mage of great promise in Dalaran before the war, a friend of Bethor Iceshard and Gunther Arcanus. The three wove their apprentice wands together into a single Woven Wand as a token of friendship. When the Lich King rose, Thule betrayed his brethren and went over to the Scourge, and he stole the wand to hide in Fenris Keep, unable to part with it though he came to despise it. With warlock and necromantic arts he brewed the ichor that animates the rot hide gnolls, and through his apparitions he promises them a war carried to the Forsaken capital itself.', 'quest 446 description (young promising mage, betrayed his brethren, allied with the Scourge); quest 491 description and reward text (Woven Wand); quest 444 description; creature_text 2056 (bring the tides of war to their very capital); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Thule_Ravenclaw; codex_tirisfal.json Gunther Arcanus entry'),
(13022, 2, 130, 6, 2, 0, 'Rane and Quinn Yorick', 'Rane and Quinn Yorick are Deathstalkers, sister and brother, sent to scout the farms of northern Silverpine and report to High Executor Hadrec. Weeks passed without word. Their mission foundered at the Ivar Patch, where the ghoul Ivar the Foul fell on them and mauled Quinn badly. The pair escaped into the farmhouse, and Rane has stood guard ever since, watching for Ivar''s return while her brother heals. A third member of their team, Erland, was cut off at Malden''s Orchard by hungry wolves. Rane still means to get their report back to the Sepulcher, for it holds information vital to the Forsaken hold on Silverpine.', 'quest 428 description (a couple of weeks without word); quest 425 description; quest 429 description; quest 430 completion text (my sister); quest_greeting 1950; quest 435 description (my teammate Rane); quest 449 description; creature_text 1950, 1951'),
(13023, 2, 130, 7, 2, 0, 'Alaric', 'Alaric was once head servant and bodyguard to Thule Ravenclaw in Fenris Keep. When the plague came, his master cast a spell meant to protect him from undeath, and instead bound him to an unlife from which he cannot escape. After creating the rot hide gnolls, Thule cut off Alaric''s head and gave it to the gnolls as a plaything, and they carry the talking head about Fenris Isle still. Alaric asks only to be reunited with his body in its hasty grave by the stable, and to rest within the keep where he spent the best days of his life. He knows where Thule hid the Woven Wand.', 'quest 460 description and completion text; quest 461 description and reward text; quest 491 description; item 3317 A Talking Head drops from Rot Hide gnolls on Fenris Isle (Horde only, conditions team 67)'),
(13024, 2, 130, 8, 0, 0, 'Nightlash', 'Nightlash is a banshee of the Scourge who haunts the Dead Field in northern Silverpine. She guards the rot hide gnolls, servants of the Scourge, who make their base on the old farm, and each time the Forsaken have sent a small force against it she has appeared at the gnolls'' side and used her magic to rout the attackers. High Executor Hadrec wants her destroyed, for the Forsaken cannot break the rot hides while she defends them. When she finally falls, her essence crumbles to dust.', 'quest 437 description and reward text; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/The_Dead_Field; DB spawn Nightlash 1983 at the Dead Field, faction template 70 (hostile to all)'),
(13025, 3, 130, 1, 2, 0, 'Arugal''s Folly', 'To Dalar Dawnweaver, the curse on Silverpine is the work of one fool. Lady Sylvanas has charged Varimathras with conquering the lands to the south, and Arugal''s reckless magic stands in the way. Dalar tests newcomers against the Moonrage worgen near the Sepulcher, then sends them to Valgan''s Field for the spell Arugal called his Remedy, and among the gluttons and darksouls for the enchanted shackles that strengthen it. While he studies, Grimson the Pale must be beheaded so that the Deep Elem Mine can serve the Forsaken. The shackles of Pyrewood complete his research, explaining why its people are human by day and worgen by night. In the village, the Deathstalker Faerleia ambushes the Pyrewood Council, Arugal''s puppets, hoping his creatures will turn on him once they are gone. At last Dalar sends champions into Shadowfang Keep for the head of Arugal himself.', 'quests 421, 422, 423, 424, 99 (descriptions and reward texts); quest 452 description and reward text; quest 1014 description; creature_queststarter: 1938 starts 421-424, 99, 1014; 2058 starts 452'),
(13026, 3, 130, 2, 2, 0, 'The Lost Deathstalkers', 'The Deathstalkers Rane and Quinn Yorick were sent to scout the northern farms and never reported back, and High Executor Hadrec wanted their fate confirmed. They are found holed up at the Ivar Patch, Quinn mauled by the ghoul Ivar the Foul. Apothecary Renferrel brews a healing draught from the discolored hearts of worgs, and once Quinn has drunk it, Ivar must be hunted down in his barn. Meanwhile their teammate Erland is trapped at Malden''s Orchard by wolves and must be escorted back through the trees. When the report reaches Hadrec at last, he admits the Scourge in Silverpine are stronger than he had reckoned. The worg hearts prove interesting too: their strange toxicity sends samples to the Undercity and on to an apothecary at the Crossroads in the Barrens.', 'quests 428, 429, 430, 425, 435, 449 (descriptions and reward texts); quests 3221, 1359, 1358 descriptions; creature_text 1978'),
(13027, 3, 130, 3, 2, 0, 'The Ravenclaw Menace', 'The rot hide gnolls first troubled the Forsaken from the Dead Field, where the banshee Nightlash broke every assault until she was destroyed. The trail then led to the Decrepit Ferry, where a boat heaped with wrapped corpses pointed across Lordamere Lake to Fenris Isle. Apothecary Renferrel studied the ichor in the gnolls'' bodies and found warlock and necromantic magic he could not fully unravel. In the Undercity, Bethor Iceshard knew the work at once: it was the craft of his old colleague Thule Ravenclaw, a promising mage who had sided with the Lich King. Bethor supplied incantations for a potion to counter Thule''s spells, and with it and arms from Hadrec''s arsenal the Forsaken struck Fenris Isle. When Thule fell, the energies released were felt even at the Sepulcher. Meanwhile Shadow Priest Allister''s scouts found more of Thule''s servants hiding at Beren''s Peril.', 'quests 437, 438, 443, 444, 446, 448, 442 (descriptions and reward texts); creature_text 1498; quest 516 description; Tirisfal writer: graverobbers trail (444, 446) continues from codex_tirisfal.json The Graverobbers'),
(13028, 3, 130, 4, 2, 0, 'Deliah''s Ring', 'Among the corpses in the boat at the Decrepit Ferry, one hand lies unwrapped: a woman''s, pocked by plague but recently dead, and on it a ring engraved For Deliah. Hadrec guesses the body came from the mass graves of Tirisfal, and Magistrate Sevren in Brill confirms that a Deliah of Brill was laid in that mass grave. Her husband Raleigh, once a chef, now dwells in the Undercity. He knows the ring but feels nothing for his dead wife. One desire still burns in him. Valdred Moray, once his good friend, was Deliah''s murderer, and has fled to the Greymane Wall hoping to slip into Gilneas. Raleigh wants Valdred dead and his hands brought back. When they arrive he gives away the ring as a worthless bauble and keeps the hands instead, as a remembrance of his friend''s betrayal.', 'quests 439, 440, 441, 530 (descriptions and reward texts); creature_template 2050 subname Ex-Chef; gameobject_queststarter 1593 starts 439; quest 440 reward text (Sevren)'),
(13029, 3, 130, 5, 2, 0, 'Dalaran''s Intentions', 'The Forsaken could not see why the wizards of Dalaran cared about a backwater like Ambermill. Shadow Priest Allister had one of their supply crates raided at a camp north of Pyrewood, and inside lay old maps of western Lordaeron and a rune-inscribed pendant. Dalar Dawnweaver knew it at once as an artifact the Kirin Tor use to channel great energies, and so many of them meant a project of real magnitude. Then he remembered: Ambermill had been earmarked by the Kirin Tor for its dormant ley energy node, and the wizards meant to wake it. Allister ordered the pendants stripped from the conjurers, mages and protectors to slow the weaving, but it was already far along, guided by an archmage of great power. Only his death could halt it. When Archmage Ataeric fell, the ley energies faded back into dormancy, though Allister warned that such power so close at hand demands plans for the future.', 'quests 477, 478, 481, 482, 479, 480 (descriptions and reward texts); DB: Archmage Ataeric 2120 drops Ataeric''s Staff 3515, quest 480 required item; gameobject 1627 Dalaran Crate at the camp north of Pyrewood'),
(13030, 3, 130, 6, 2, 0, 'A Recipe for Death', 'The Royal Apothecary Society labors under heavy pressure from the Dark Lady to produce a New Plague, one that could wipe out both the Scourge and the humans of Lordaeron. Apothecary Renferrel believes Silverpine holds the ingredients. Spider blood from the Skittering Dark, mixed with toxin from the hearts of grizzled bears, yields a deadly elixir for Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity. More promising still are the findings of Apothecary Berard, one of the Society''s brightest, whom Arugal''s curse turned into a mindless servant. His journal, taken from his study in the Pyrewood inn, describes an ancient plague that killed all the aquatic life in Lordamere Lake, and points to the moss of the lake''s skulkers and creepers and a rare tumor found on a Vile Fin murloc. Faranell declares the Society on the cusp of something great, and Renferrel sends his findings on to Tarren Mill.', 'quests 447, 450, 451 (descriptions and reward texts); quest 493 description; quest_greeting 2055');
